Interpret terminals on the arm64 backend, through UserCallbacks::InterpreterFallback

Why: the A64 frontend ends a block with an Interpret terminal at an instruction it does not
decode (the ARMv8.1 LDADD and LDAPR the client uses, emulator/src/runtime.rs on_fallback), and
the arm64 backend stopped with "Interpret should never be emitted." Done as the x64 backend does
it: the guest's state is all in A64JitState at the terminal, so the PC is stored, the callback
runs with (pc, num_instructions) through a prelude trampoline like CallSVC's, and the run returns.
emulator/src/cpu.rs's an_undecoded_instruction_reaches_the_fallback checks it.

Upstream: azahar-emu/dynarmic a46601580d55 (its master on 2026-11-12) lacks this; it is not
sent upstream.

